# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Vite bakes VITE_-prefixed variables into the build at BUILD TIME, not at
# server runtime like the backend's .env. There is no "set it on the host
# and restart" for these — if you don't set this before running `npm run
# build`, the production bundle silently falls back to the page's own host
# (see client/src/lib/apiClient.ts), which will not be reachable from a real
# deployment.
#
# Copy this file to .env.production (or .env) and set the real API origin
# before building for deployment.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.your-production-domain.com


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LAN hosting during local development
#
#   npm run dev       loopback only — http://localhost:3000
#   npm run dev:lan   also on the Wi-Fi, for testing on a real phone or tablet
#
# `dev:lan` passes `--host`, and Vite prints a "Network:" URL on startup.
# ⚠️ Open THAT URL on the device. `localhost` on a phone means the phone.
#
# You do not need to set anything below for this to work. With no
# VITE_API_BASE_URL, the client derives the API origin from whatever host the
# page was loaded from — so a page served at http://192.168.1.42:3000 calls
# http://192.168.1.42:5000, while localhost keeps calling localhost.
#
# The API server already listens on all interfaces, and CORS accepts private
# -network origins when NODE_ENV is not production (server/src/config/
# cors.config.ts). In production the ALLOWED_ORIGINS allowlist is the only
# way in — that guard is the safety property and must not be softened.
#
# ⚠️ LAN hosting is opt-in per command, not a config default, because this dev
# server renders real seeded patient records behind a real login. Do not run
# `dev:lan` on a café, hotel or client network.
#
# Only set this if your API is NOT on port 5000 of the same host:
# VITE_API_PORT=5000
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
